# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: cador-tests-reference-builtins-core-without-depending-on-it -- clautolisp/cador/tests does not compile unless the builtins were loaded first
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: infra
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: fix-cador-tests-reference-builtins-core-without-depending-on-it

* Context

Found 2026-10-07 while reproducing
install-core-builtins-leaks-com-hooks-across-suites (closed).

* Symptom

In a fresh SBCL, loading the cador test system before the builtins:

#+begin_src lisp
(asdf:load-asd (merge-pathnames "clautolisp.asd" (uiop:getcwd)))
(asdf:load-system "clautolisp/tests")   ; or (asdf:test-system "clautolisp/cador")
#+end_src

fails with a COMPILE-FILE-ERROR on =cador/tests/registry-native-tests.lisp=:

#+begin_example
READ error during COMPILE-FILE:
  Package CLAUTOLISP.AUTOLISP-BUILTINS-CORE does not exist.
  Line: 61, Column: 81
#+end_example

=make test-sbcl= does not see it because it runs
=(asdf:test-system "clautolisp")=, which loads the aggregate system (and so
the builtins) before the test systems.

* Cause

=cador/tests/registry-native-tests.lisp= lines 61-66 call
=clautolisp.autolisp-builtins-core::%registry-value->autolisp=, but the
=clautolisp/cador/tests= system depends only on ="clautolisp/cador"= and
="fiveam"=. The test exercises the builtins' conversion of native registry
values, so either the system needs ="clautolisp/autolisp-builtins-core"= in
its =:depends-on=, or that check belongs in the builtins-core suite.

* Acceptance criteria

- =(asdf:test-system "clautolisp/cador")= in a fresh image compiles and
  runs the cador suite.

* Resolution (2026-10-07, clautolisp 2.2.228)

=clautolisp/cador/tests= now depends on ="clautolisp/autolisp-builtins-core"=
(the test checks the builtins' conversion of native registry values, so it
needs them; there is no cycle: builtins-core does not depend on cador).
Reproduced before the fix in a fresh SBCL (=(asdf:load-system
"clautolisp/cador/tests")= -> COMPILE-FILE-ERROR, "Package
CLAUTOLISP.AUTOLISP-BUILTINS-CORE does not exist"); after it,
=(asdf:test-system "clautolisp/cador")= in a fresh image runs the cador suite:
1574 checks, Fail 0.

